pragma silverscript ^0.1.0;

// A covered account (docs/ARCHITECTURE-CLEARING.md 13): its user's coins and its legs, and nothing of the clearing
// side: the other side is its shard's books. A leg's entry stays. Three kinds of statement are stated on it
// (KpfTChange): the user takes coins out (7), legs leave by the user's statement (8), a step of the user's
// liquidation (9). What is stated: the amount (a take's; a step's fee) and the leg that leaves (0 none, -1 every
// leg), 8 bytes each; the chain of the leg that leaves alone (blake2b(32 zero bytes + the leg): what its note names
// it by); then a trace, a row of 120 bytes a leg (the price, six sums, two chains):
//   a_i    the price stated for leg i
//   G_i    what the legs 1..i gained or lost at the prices stated            (the user's standing is of this net)
//   W_i    what they are worth
//   WS_i   what those of them that stay are worth
//   LS_i   what those that stay have lost, each counted alone                (a gain of a leg that stays is no coin)
//   GL_i   what those that leave gained or lost
//   g_i    the chain of the legs up to i          h_i    the chain of those that stay, their entries as they are
// A dispute names one point (KpfTPoint): 2i - 1 row i (KpfTCRow), 2i the price of row i (KpfTStepPrice), 0 the end
// (KpfTCEnd). A point nobody answers costs the claimer its bond: the prices are the claimer's to show.
//
// KpfTCEnd: the answer of the point 0. The end is right when the last row's chain is the account's legs', the
// account has nothing of a second party's, and by the last row's sums (m: the user's coins less a note's least,
// which stays with the user whatever happens and is no coin of the account's in any test; up: the maintenance
// rate and the tolerance; the band: twice the tolerance of what the legs that leave are worth; R: what the legs can
// lose by a move of `up`, legs of one market next to one another counted together, of all the legs and of those that
// stay, the last group closed here: docs 17.4, 17.8h). The statement's head (the rate, the tolerance, T) is held to
// the terms and the account's times.
// The account's moving part has, where a position has its asks, the legs counted and the time before which its
// user states nothing again. A take and a leaving are stated at or after that time, and write their own time and
// twice the longest a statement lives; a step is held to no time and writes none (docs 14.2).
//   7, a take (the user's key; no leg leaves): the coins that stay are at R and at LS. (Of an account of
//      no leg: stated with no row.) outs: the account with the amount less; the amount to the user.
//   8, a leaving (the user's key). Of every leg (-1): the account ends. Of one leg that gained: the coins are at
//      R of what stays and at LS. Of one that lost: the coins pay what it lost, and with G they are at R of what
//      stays (the level of an entry). (The account's only leg leaving alone leaves an account of no leg.)
//   9, a step (anyone; the fee is stated): due by the prices its rows say, each within the lower rate of its row's:
//      the coins and what a step would leave of G and of what the legs gain to those prices (less the band where
//      it is above nothing) are below nothing. The leg named lost: it leaves alone where the account lacks less
//      without it (R and what it has, before and after) and the coins pay it, its fee no more than the coins hold
//      beyond what it lost and what the legs that stay lost (review 47); an account that holds tokens is not
//      taken whole: the leg leaves alone, owing what the coins do not pay. Else every leg leaves, for the fee of
//      W, of what is left when the loss is paid. Named a leg that gained while another lost: wrong.
// Where one leg leaves: the account without it (the second chain), its coins less what the leg lost and the fee;
// the fee to the claimer; and the note that the leg left: what the shard is asked (what it gained beyond the band;
// below zero what it lost, and the note holds those coins).
// Where every leg leaves: G >= 0, the shard is asked G beyond the band; G < 0, the coins pay what was lost as far
// as they go, a note's least staying with the user. Then the fee, of what is left. outs: what the account held,
// less those, to the user; the fee; the note, of the account's own chain.
//   answer(who, ageb, slotLen, terms, root, moving, kind, t0, said, outs, bond, claimer, window, late, held, dkey,
//          point, at, rkey, verdict)                                                                           anyone.
contract KpfTCEnd(int init_version) {
    int version = init_version;

    int constant SIDE_A = 1;
    int constant SIDE_B = 2;
    int constant BPS = 10000;
    int constant MMR_AT = 10;
    int constant G_AT = 19;
    int constant LIQFEE_AT = 28;
    // What every operation leaves in the copy it used, for whoever the prices are from (KpfTSweep, KpfTPay).
    int constant ORACLE_FEE = 200000;
    int constant STATE_AT = 2;
    int constant CHANGE_TAG = 10;
    int constant POINT_TAG = 11;
    int constant NOTE_TAG = 12;
    // The least a note holds.
    int constant NOTE_MIN = 20000000;
    // The lateness of a statement that stands again after a point of it was answered right: it was held to its time
    // when it was disputed, and is not held to it again.
    int constant LATE_AGAIN = 499999999999;

    function p33(byte[32] h) : byte[] {
        return byte[](0x20) + byte[](h);
    }

    function i9(int c) : byte[] {
        return byte[](0x08) + byte[](c as byte[8]);
    }

    function slotOf(int j, int slotLen) : byte[] {
        require(j >= 0);
        require(j < tx.inputs.length);
        require(j != this.activeInputIndex);
        int len = OpTxInputScriptSigLen(j);
        require(slotLen > STATE_AT + 32);
        require(slotLen <= len);
        byte[] rs = OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(j, len - slotLen, len);
        require(tx.inputs[j].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SHFromRedeemScript(rs)));
        return rs;
    }

    // The answer of a point. The point is right (1), by anyone's answer: the statement stands again (its dispute
    // period begins again; another point of it may be disputed until the last time to dispute; it is not held to
    // its time again), and the disputer's bond is lost: a quarter to the claimer (the last output), a quarter to
    // whoever answered (the one before), half to this script's copy (a claimer that answers its own other key's
    // dispute loses half a bond a round: docs 14.1).
    // The point is wrong (0): the position again, the disputer's bond back (the output before the last) and half of
    // the claimer's to whoever answered (the last). The other half of the bond lost stays in this script's copy.
    function ends(int j, byte[] rs, int slotLen, int verdict, byte[32] c0, byte[32] position, int bond, byte[32] claimer, byte[32] dkey, byte[32] rkey) {
        require(verdict == 0 || verdict == 1);
        require(bond > 0);
        int v = tx.inputs[j].value;
        require(v >= bond + bond);
        int half = bond / 2;
        int kept = bond - half;
        byte[32] id = OpInputCovenantId(j);
        require(OpCovInputCount(id) == 1);
        require(OpCovOutputCount(id) == 1);
        int c = OpCovOutputIdx(id, 0);
        int m = tx.outputs.length - 1 - 4 * j;
        if (verdict == 1) {
            require(tx.outputs[c].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SHFromRedeemScript(rs.slice(0, STATE_AT) + byte[](c0) + rs.slice(STATE_AT + 32, slotLen))));
            require(tx.outputs[c].value >= v - bond);
            require(m >= tx.inputs.length);
            // (Two outputs of less than this fit in no transaction: where a quarter is no payable amount the
            // claimer has half, in one output, and nobody is paid for the answer. Review 50, F77.)
            if (bond / 4 >= 5000000) {
                require(m - 1 >= tx.inputs.length);
                half = bond / 4;
                kept = bond - half - half;
                require(tx.outputs[m - 1].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2PK(pubkey(rkey))));
                require(tx.outputs[m - 1].value >= half);
            }
            rkey = claimer;
        } else {
            require(tx.outputs[c].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SHFromRedeemScript(rs.slice(0, STATE_AT) + byte[](position) + rs.slice(STATE_AT + 32, slotLen))));
            require(tx.outputs[c].value >= v - bond - bond);
            require(m - 1 >= tx.inputs.length);
            require(tx.outputs[m - 1].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2PK(pubkey(dkey))));
            require(tx.outputs[m - 1].value >= bond);
        }
        if (half > 0) {
            require(tx.outputs[m].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2PK(pubkey(rkey))));
            require(tx.outputs[m].value >= half);
        }
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        byte[32] lib = OpInputCovenantId(self);
        require(tx.outputs[self].scriptPubKey == tx.inputs[self].scriptPubKey);
        require(OpOutputCovenantId(self) == lib);
        require(tx.outputs[self].value >= tx.inputs[self].value + ORACLE_FEE + kept);
        require(OpCovOutputCount(lib) == OpCovInputCount(lib));
    }

    entry answer(byte[24] who, byte[8] ageb, int slotLen, byte[90] terms, byte[32] root, byte[171] moving, int kind, int t0, byte[] said, byte[32] outs, int bond, byte[32] claimer, int window, int late, int held, byte[32] dkey, int point, int at, byte[32] rkey, int verdict) {
        byte[] mv = byte[](moving);
        byte[] tb = byte[](terms);
        byte[32] position = blake2b(p33(blake2b(tb + p33(root))) + mv);
        require(version == 1);
        require(int(ageb) >= 0);
        int j = int(byte[8](who.slice(0, 8)));
        byte[] rs = slotOf(j, slotLen);
        require(said.length >= 80);
        int amount = int(byte[8](said.slice(0, 8)));
        int skip = int(byte[8](said.slice(8, 16)));
        byte[] rows = said.slice(80, said.length);
        byte[] pre = i9(CHANGE_TAG) + p33(position) + i9(kind) + i9(t0) + p33(blake2b(said)) + p33(outs) + i9(bond) + p33(claimer) + i9(window);
        byte[32] c0 = blake2b(pre + i9(late) + i9(held));
        // (A statement that stands again keeps its lateness, beside the mark that it does: the last time to dispute
        // it is counted from its time by it.)
        int again = late;
        if (late < LATE_AGAIN) { again = LATE_AGAIN + late; }
        byte[32] c1 = blake2b(pre + i9(again) + i9(held));
        require(blake2b(i9(POINT_TAG) + p33(c0) + p33(dkey) + i9(point)) == byte[32](rs.slice(STATE_AT, STATE_AT + 32)));
        require(at == point || verdict == 0);
        int n = rows.length / 232;
        require(rows.length == 232 * n);
        require(at == 0);
        require(who.slice(8, 16) == who.slice(0, 8));
        require(who.slice(16, 24) == who.slice(0, 8));
        require(kind >= 7);
        require(kind <= 9);
        byte[] z32 = byte[](0 as byte[8]) + byte[](0 as byte[8]) + byte[](0 as byte[8]) + byte[](0 as byte[8]);
        byte[] row = z32 + z32 + z32 + z32 + z32 + z32 + z32 + byte[](0 as byte[8]);
        if (n >= 1) {
            row = rows.slice(232 * (n - 1), 232 * n);
        }
        int gain = int(byte[8](row.slice(8, 16)));
        int w = int(byte[8](row.slice(16, 24)));
        int ws = int(byte[8](row.slice(24, 32)));
        int ls = int(byte[8](row.slice(32, 40)));
        int gl = int(byte[8](row.slice(40, 48)));
        int ok = 1;
        if (n < 1) {
            // (An account of no leg takes a take, stated with no row.)
            if (kind != 7) { ok = 0; }
        }
        if (byte[32](row.slice(168, 200)) != root) { ok = 0; }
        if (w < 0) { ok = 0; }
        if (ws < 0) { ok = 0; }
        if (ws > w) { ok = 0; }
        if (ls < 0) { ok = 0; }
        // (What the token legs that stay count, as coins: docs 16.12.)
        int tk = int(byte[8](row.slice(48, 56)));
        if (tk < 0) { ok = 0; }
        // The user's coins, and nothing of a second party's. A note's least of them is no coin of the account's:
        // it stays with the user where every leg leaves (`m` is the coins less it).
        int coins = int(byte[8](mv.slice(67, 75)));
        int m = coins - NOTE_MIN;
        // (What the account owes its shard, where a position has side B's margin: docs 16.18. An account that owes
        // takes a step, and nothing else of these kinds.)
        int owes = int(byte[8](mv.slice(76, 84)));
        if (owes < 0) { ok = 0; }
        if (owes != 0) {
            if (kind != 9) { ok = 0; }
        }
        int g = int(byte[8](tb.slice(G_AT, G_AT + 8)));
        int up = int(byte[8](tb.slice(MMR_AT, MMR_AT + 8))) + g;
        // The head of the statement (docs 17.8h): the rate, the tolerance and T that its rows computed with are the
        // terms' and the account's, or the end is wrong.
        if (int(byte[8](said.slice(48, 56))) != up) { ok = 0; }
        if (int(byte[8](said.slice(56, 64))) != g) { ok = 0; }
        if (int(byte[8](said.slice(64, 72))) != 2 * (int(byte[8](mv.slice(94, 102))) + int(byte[8](mv.slice(103, 111))))) { ok = 0; }
        // What is asked: R of the groups that are closed, and of the last what the larger of its two sums lost.
        int rall = int(byte[8](row.slice(104, 112)));
        if (0 - int(byte[8](row.slice(88, 96))) > 0 - int(byte[8](row.slice(96, 104)))) {
            if (int(byte[8](row.slice(88, 96))) < 0) { rall = rall - int(byte[8](row.slice(88, 96))); }
        } else {
            if (int(byte[8](row.slice(96, 104))) < 0) { rall = rall - int(byte[8](row.slice(96, 104))); }
        }
        int rst = int(byte[8](row.slice(128, 136)));
        if (0 - int(byte[8](row.slice(112, 120))) > 0 - int(byte[8](row.slice(120, 128)))) {
            if (int(byte[8](row.slice(112, 120))) < 0) { rst = rst - int(byte[8](row.slice(112, 120))); }
        } else {
            if (int(byte[8](row.slice(120, 128))) < 0) { rst = rst - int(byte[8](row.slice(120, 128))); }
        }
        // Where a position has its asks: the legs counted, and the time before which the user states nothing
        // again. A statement of the user's writes its own time and twice the longest a statement lives (the
        // lateness and two dispute periods): between two of them the account is free for a step.
        int count = int(byte[8](mv.slice(121, 129)));
        int quiet = int(byte[8](mv.slice(130, 138)));
        int next = t0 + 2 * (int(byte[8](mv.slice(94, 102))) + 2 * int(byte[8](mv.slice(103, 111))));
        int when = quiet;
        if (kind != 9) {
            if (t0 < quiet) { ok = 0; }
            when = next;
        }
        byte[] due = byte[](0x00);
        if (kind == 7) {
            if (skip != 0) { ok = 0; }
            if (byte[](claimer) != mv.slice(1, 33)) { ok = 0; }
            if (amount <= 0) { ok = 0; }
            if (ok == 1) {
                // (No more than the coins: what a token leg counts leaves no coin that is not there.)
                if (m - amount < 0) { ok = 0; }
                if (m - amount + tk < rall + ls) { ok = 0; }
            }
            if (ok == 1) {
                due = byte[](0x00) + byte[](blake2b(p33(blake2b(tb + p33(root))) + mv.slice(0, 67) + byte[]((coins - amount) as byte[8]) + mv.slice(75, 130) + byte[](when as byte[8]) + mv.slice(138, 171))) + byte[]((held - amount) as byte[8]) + byte[](0x01) + byte[](claimer) + byte[](amount as byte[8]);
            }
        } else {
            int all = 0;
            if (skip == 0 - 1) { all = 1; }
            if (skip == 0) { ok = 0; }
            if (skip < 0 - 1) { ok = 0; }
            if (skip > n) { ok = 0; }
            if (kind == 8) {
                if (byte[](claimer) != mv.slice(1, 33)) { ok = 0; }
            } else {
                if (skip < 1) { ok = 0; }
            }
            int fee = 0;
            int owing = 0;
            int setoff = 0;
            int wl = 0;
            int liq = int(byte[8](tb.slice(LIQFEE_AT, LIQFEE_AT + 8)));
            if (ok == 1) {
                wl = w - ws;
                if (kind == 8) {
                    if (all == 0) {
                        if (gl >= 0) {
                            if (m + tk < rst + ls) { ok = 0; }
                        } else {
                            if (m + gl < 0) { ok = 0; }
                            // (What stays is at the level of an entry: without the leg it may be asked more.
                            // docs 17.4, N65.)
                            if (m + gain + tk < rst) { ok = 0; }
                        }
                    }
                } else {
                    // Due by the prices the rows say (each within the lower rate of its row's): what a step would
                    // leave the account is below nothing. What the legs gained to those prices counts less the
                    // band where it is above nothing, and no less than nothing (docs 17.8g, D).
                    int sx = gain + int(byte[8](row.slice(64, 72)));
                    if (sx >= 0) {
                        sx = sx - ((w / BPS) * (g + g) + ((w % BPS) * (g + g) + BPS - 1) / BPS);
                        if (sx < 0) { sx = 0; }
                    }
                    if (m + tk - owes + sx >= 0) { ok = 0; }
                }
            }
            if (ok == 1) {
                if (kind == 9) {
                    if (all == 0) {
                        if (gl < 0) {
                            // The leg named lost: it leaves alone where the account lacks less after it than
                            // before (docs 17.4), its fee no more than the coins hold beyond what it lost and
                            // what the legs that stay lost.
                            fee = (wl / BPS) * liq + ((wl % BPS) * liq) / BPS;
                            int cap = m + gl - ls;
                            if (cap < 0) { cap = 0; }
                            if (fee > cap) { fee = cap; }
                            int bf = rall - (m + tk - owes) - gain;
                            if (bf < 0) { bf = 0; }
                            // (Counted before the fee: a fee does not turn a step of one leg into one of every leg.
                            // Review T13, W2.)
                            int af = rst - (m + tk - owes + gain);
                            if (af < 0) { af = 0; }
                            if (tk != 0) {
                                // (An account that holds tokens is not taken whole: the leg named leaves alone,
                                // and the account owes what the coins do not pay. docs 16.18; review T13, W1.)
                                if (m + gl < 0) { owing = 1; }
                            } else if (af >= bf || m + gl < 0) {
                                // (The account does not lack less without the leg, or the coins do not pay it.)
                                all = 1;
                            }
                        } else {
                            if (ls != 0) { ok = 0; }
                            if (tk != 0) {
                                fee = (wl / BPS) * liq + ((wl % BPS) * liq) / BPS;
                            } else {
                                all = 1;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    if (all == 1) {
                        fee = (w / BPS) * liq + ((w % BPS) * liq) / BPS;
                    }
                }
            }
            // (Not every leg while the account holds a token leg: its tokens leave, or are sold, first.)
            if (all == 1) {
                if (tk != 0) { ok = 0; }
            }
            if (ok == 1) {
                int g2 = g + g;
                int pay = 0;
                int asked = 0;
                if (all == 1) {
                    int room = m;
                    if (room < 0) { room = 0; }
                    if (gain < 0) {
                        pay = 0 - gain;
                        if (pay > room) { pay = room; }
                        asked = 0 - pay;
                    } else {
                        asked = gain - ((w / BPS) * g2 + ((w % BPS) * g2 + BPS - 1) / BPS);
                        if (asked < 0) { asked = 0; }
                        // (What the account owes its shard is set against what its legs ask of it: review 64, F112.)
                        if (asked > owes) { asked = asked - owes; } else { asked = 0; }
                    }
                    if (fee > room - pay) { fee = room - pay; }
                    due = byte[](0x01) + mv.slice(1, 33) + byte[]((held - pay - fee) as byte[8]);
                    if (fee > 0) {
                        due = due + byte[](0x01) + byte[](claimer) + byte[](fee as byte[8]);
                    }
                    due = due + byte[](0x02) + byte[](blake2b(i9(NOTE_TAG) + mv.slice(138, 171) + i9(6) + p33(root) + mv.slice(0, 33) + i9(asked))) + byte[]((NOTE_MIN + pay) as byte[8]);
                } else {
                    if (gl < 0) {
                        pay = 0 - gl;
                        asked = gl;
                    } else {
                        asked = gl - ((wl / BPS) * g2 + ((wl % BPS) * g2 + BPS - 1) / BPS);
                        if (asked < 0) { asked = 0; }
                        // (What the account owes its shard is set against what the leg asks of it: the account
                        // owes that much less. Review 64, F112.)
                        setoff = asked;
                        if (setoff > owes) { setoff = owes; }
                        asked = asked - setoff;
                    }
                    // An account that holds tokens and whose coins do not pay the leg: the coins pay what they can
                    // of what it lost, then of the fee, and the account owes the rest. It writes the account's
                    // time: a sale of what it holds is stated at or after it.
                    int more = 0;
                    more = 0 - setoff;
                    int room1 = m;
                    if (room1 < 0) { room1 = 0; }
                    if (owing == 1) {
                        more = pay;
                        if (pay > room1) { pay = room1; }
                        more = more - pay;
                        asked = 0 - pay;
                        int grace = t0 + int(byte[8](mv.slice(94, 102))) + int(byte[8](mv.slice(103, 111)));
                        if (when < grace) { when = grace; }
                    }
                    if (fee > room1 - pay) { fee = room1 - pay; }
                    due = byte[](0x00) + byte[](blake2b(p33(blake2b(tb + byte[](0x20) + row.slice(200, 232))) + mv.slice(0, 67) + byte[]((coins - pay - fee) as byte[8]) + mv.slice(75, 76) + byte[]((owes + more) as byte[8]) + mv.slice(84, 121) + byte[]((count - 1) as byte[8]) + mv.slice(129, 130) + byte[](when as byte[8]) + mv.slice(138, 171))) + byte[]((held - pay - fee) as byte[8]);
                    if (fee > 0) {
                        due = due + byte[](0x01) + byte[](claimer) + byte[](fee as byte[8]);
                    }
                    due = due + byte[](0x02) + byte[](blake2b(i9(NOTE_TAG) + mv.slice(138, 171) + i9(6) + byte[](0x20) + said.slice(16, 48) + mv.slice(0, 33) + i9(asked))) + byte[]((NOTE_MIN + pay) as byte[8]);
                }
                if (amount != fee) { ok = 0; }
            }
        }
        if (ok == 1) {
            if (blake2b(due) != outs) { ok = 0; }
        }
        require(ok == verdict);
        ends(j, rs, slotLen, verdict, c1, position, bond, claimer, dkey, rkey);
    }

    // The copy lets go of what gathered in it: a script of the library names it at a place, as an object is named
    // (KpfSlot.go asks no more), and answers for the rest. Only KpfTSweep's entry passes with a copy at a place it
    // names (every other entry holds what it names to the hash of an object's state), and it asks that the copy goes
    // on as it is, under the library's id, with what a copy keeps.
    entry release(int l, int k) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        require(k >= 0);
        require(k <= 2);
        // (An input that is not there has no id: the engine refuses the index.)
        require(OpInputCovenantId(l) == OpInputCovenantId(self));
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(l, 0, 1) == byte[](0x18));
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(l, 1 + 8 * k, 9 + 8 * k) == byte[](self as byte[8]));
    }
}
